{%- liquid
  assign rs_opt = product.options_with_values | where: 'name', 'Colour' | first
  if rs_opt == blank
    assign rs_opt = product.options_with_values | first
  endif
-%}
{%- liquid
  assign rs_v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign rs_unit = rs_v.price
  assign rs_cmp = rs_v.compare_at_price | default: rs_v.price
  comment
    Preview-only: draft products can't be opened on the storefront, so the preview theme's
    rainsong-6inch-demo template renders this page on another product at the 6-inch price.
    Never true on the real 6-inch template.
  endcomment
  if template.suffix == 'rainsong-6inch-demo'
    assign rs_unit = 9999
    assign rs_cmp = 9999
  endif
  comment
    RRP per drum (owner t141u/t142u/t143u): every "was" price and % off on this page is based on this RRP x quantity
    (US $150, UK £120). Product compare-at is set to the same values so Kaching and the cart match.
    To remove: delete from here to the matching endif below (the page falls back to the product compare-at price).
  endcomment
  assign rs_rrp = 0
  if cart.currency.iso_code == 'USD'
    assign rs_rrp = 15000
  elsif cart.currency.iso_code == 'GBP'
    assign rs_rrp = 12000
  endif
  if rs_rrp > rs_cmp
    assign rs_cmp = rs_rrp
  endif
  assign rs_head = rs_heading | default: 'Margaret’s Rain Drum'
  comment
    Pack totals (owner t128u), same as the Kaching deals. These are first-paint fallbacks; rainsong6.js repaints from Kaching.
    US $99.99 / $159.99 / $199.99 / $249.99. UK £79.99 / £127.99 / £159.99 / £199.99.
    % off rounds to the nearest whole number, same as Kaching (owner t142u): vs $150 RRP 33% / 47% / 56% / 58%.
  endcomment
  assign rs_t2 = 15999
  assign rs_t3 = 19999
  assign rs_t4 = 24999
  if cart.currency.iso_code == 'GBP'
    assign rs_t2 = 12799
    assign rs_t3 = 15999
    assign rs_t4 = 19999
  endif
  assign p2t = rs_t2
  assign p2 = p2t | plus: 1 | divided_by: 2
  assign p2w = rs_cmp | times: 2
  assign p2s = p2w | minus: p2t
  assign p2c = p2s | times: 100.0 | divided_by: p2w | round
  assign p1s = rs_cmp | minus: rs_unit
  assign p1c = p1s | times: 100.0 | divided_by: rs_cmp | round
-%}

